<p><strong>Booking software price in Nepal depends on how many branches you run, how big your team is and which features you need, so most vendors quote per business instead of publishing fixed tiers. Zennly is quoted per business, with no setup fees.</strong></p>

<h2>What changes the price</h2>
<p>The main drivers are the number of branches, the number of staff using the system, and the features you switch on, such as discount approval, staff transfers, reporting and payment tracking. Two businesses of different size should not pay the same.</p>

<h2>Questions to ask every vendor</h2>
<p>Ask whether there is a setup fee, whether you pay per branch, per user or per business, what is included in support and training, and whether the price changes when you open a new branch. Ask for the quote in Nepali rupees, in writing.</p>

<h2>Compare cost with what you lose today</h2>
<p>A double-booked therapist, an unapproved discount or a day nobody can reconcile all cost money. When you compare quotes, compare them with what those problems cost your business each month.</p>

<h2>How Zennly pricing works</h2>
<p>Zennly is quoted per business, based on your branches, team size and the features you use. There are no setup fees. Book a 20-minute demo and you receive a tailored quote within 24 hours. See <a href="/pricing/">how Zennly pricing works</a>.</p>

<h2>Before you decide, check</h2>
<ul>
<li>Setup fee: yes or no</li>
<li>Pricing basis: per branch, user or business</li>
<li>What changes when you add a branch</li>
<li>Support and training included</li>
<li>Whether the quote is in NPR and in writing</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to compare quotes fairly</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Ask for the same scope from each vendor:</strong> number of branches, staff, and features.</li>
<li><strong>Ask what is included</strong> in the base price and what costs extra, such as extra branches, extra users or messaging.</li>
<li><strong>Ask about setup and training:</strong> is it included, and is it in person or by video?</li>
<li><strong>Ask about changes:</strong> what happens to the price when you add a branch?</li>
<li><strong>Ask for the quote in writing,</strong> in the currency you will pay.</li>
</ol>
<h2>What not to compare</h2>
<p>Do not compare a simple diary with a full operations system on price alone. The cost of a double-booking, an unapproved discount or a missed daily close often exceeds the price difference. See <a href="/blog/discount-leakage/">discount leakage</a> and <a href="/blog/daily-reconciliation/">daily reconciliation</a>. You can <a href="/contact/">talk to us</a> for a quote within 24 hours.</p>
